    REFACTOR-0001: move the booking rules into a pure core
    
    book() did four jobs at once: read the file, decide whether a request
    breaks a rule, write the file, and word the answer. Only the second is
    about bookings, and it's the one the tests were there for.
    
    src/core/rules.ts now has refusalFor(), which takes a request and the
    day's other bookings and says why it can't be booked, or undefined if
    it can. It's plain data in, plain data out: no file, no fs, no format
    version. Booking moved into the core with it. book() still reads and
    writes the file, and asks refusalFor() in between.
    
    test/core/rules.spec.ts tests each rule with plain Booking objects and
    no double at all. The FakeFileSystem tests still pass, but they now
    test the rules a second time, through the file format.
    
    test/architecture.spec.ts is switched on: nothing in src/core may
    import anything outside src/core.

